  "description": "DEMO SCALE: 30 x 20 mm, 0.3 mm deep, one fluidic layer, resin print + hot emboss. Scaled uniformly in x and y by 0.389 (tools/fit_chip.py) from 75 x 25 mm; depths are not scaled (cell wash 0.5 -> 0.3 mm) and volume_ul is recomputed by the tool from the new geometry. Channel widths (0.078 mm after scaling) and the merge junction were clamped up to the 0.2 mm floor, which changed the flow resistances: the clamped channels are about 2.6x wider than scaled, so flow numbers from the original design must be re-derived. The serpentine mixer was resized by hand to 0.2 mm channel, 4 turns, 20.2 mm (was 0.15 mm, 10 turns, 52 mm). PORTS 8 -> 6 (limit 6, pitch >= 5 mm): m1b_cells_in_1/2/3 merged into m1b_cells_in_1, because Module 1 now drains all three lanes through one outlet (m1_out_1); the lane labels already let the pooled cells be told apart. Lost: separate per-lane cell lines (no lane can be held back). Residual: the 30 um pillar filter gap is far below the 0.2 mm printable floor and the cell-wash method is still TBC, so both are placeholders. Automated bridge from Module 1 to Module 2: quench (T-junction + serpentine), wash, filter, count at a QC window, resuspend in dextran buffer, send to Module 2's core inlet. Designed and simulated; not printed this weekend. GENERATED by cad/generators/m1b_cellprep.py (the generator still emits the 75 x 25 mm design).",
